# {{name}}

A [Morningstar]({{up}}AGENTS.md) application: one Rust crate, drawn on the
GPU, the same on Android and iOS. Made by `morningstar-new`; everything
here is yours to change.

## Commands

Run them from the repository root.

```sh
cargo test -p {{package}}                                  # the app driven with no device
cargo run -p {{package}} --example screenshot -- out/      # the screens as PNGs; look at them
tools/preview.sh {{package}}                               # live in a window on this Mac; reloads on save
MORNINGSTAR_APP={{package}} MORNINGSTAR_ABIS=arm64-v8a tools/build-android.sh --install   # onto a phone
cargo run -q -p morningstar-devtools --bin morningstar-icon -- {{package}} --preview out/icon.png   # the launcher icon in every form
```
@@if server

The server (`server/`, Node 20 or newer, no dependencies):

```sh
cd {{dir}}/{{package}}/server && npm test && npm start     # 127.0.0.1:{{port}}
adb reverse tcp:{{port}} tcp:{{port}}                      # lets a phone on USB reach it
```

A build for a deployed server names it at compile time, so the address is
never in the repository:
`{{env}}_SERVER_URL=https://... tools/build-android.sh`.
@@end

The first `cargo test` writes `tests/references/*.png`. Look at them and
commit them: they are what the screens are held to from then on.

## Where things are

| Path | Holds |
| --- | --- |
| `Cargo.toml` | The app's name, id, icon and platform services, under `[package.metadata.morningstar]`, and nowhere else |
| `src/lib.rs` | The whole app: state, messages, screens, effects |
@@if server
| `src/json.rs` | The little JSON the app reads and writes |
| `server/` | The app's server and its contract, `server/API.md` |
@@end
| `tests/e2e.rs` | Journeys made with taps and keys |
| `tests/accessibility.rs` | Every screen passes the accessibility check |
| `tests/screens.rs` | What the screens look like, against `tests/references/` |
| `examples/screenshot.rs` | Renders the screens to PNGs |
| `assets/icon.png` | The launcher icon's source, 1024 x 1024. Replace it with your own |
| `assets/fonts/` | Noto Sans (SIL Open Font License, `OFL.txt`) |
| `design/` | Where a design's reference pictures go; `design/README.md` |
| `SCREENS.md` | The screens and what each control does |

## How the app is written

- `view` draws the state; it changes nothing. `update` changes the state
  for one message; it draws nothing and does no I/O.
- Work that takes time (a request, a stored value, sound, a live room) is
  asked for in `effects` and comes back as a message (ADR 0019). Tests
  answer it with `Ui::testing`, which is why they need no phone.
- Sizes are in dp. Give a widget an `id` when a test needs to find it or it
  keeps state (scroll position, focus).
- After changing anything visual, render a screenshot and look at it.

